  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-fall-2021-p8.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "We know \\[\\begin{aligned}16,383 &= 16384-1 \\\\&= 2^{14}-1 \\\\&= (2^7-1)(2^7+1) \\\\&= 127\\cdot 129.\\end{aligned}\\] Since \\(129=3\\cdot 43,\\) we get \\[16383 = 3\\cdot 43\\cdot 127.\\] Therefore, \\(127\\) is the largest prime factor, and the sum of its digits is \\(10.\\)\n\nThus, the answer is C .",
      "hints": [
        "\\(16383=2^{14}-1\\)",
        "Use \\(2^{14}-1=(2^7-1)(2^7+1)\\)"
      ],
